==English==

===Idiom===
'''[[down]] [[pat]]'''
#{{idiom}} Thoroughly [[practiced]], [[rehearsed]] or [[understood]].
#:''After 2 years of the routine, they have it '''down pat''', so that they don't even have to look to complete it anymore.''

Origin: Arguably arising from the American Football term, P.A.T., or "point after touchdown." This is an extra-point procedure (see [[American football]]) which is nearly always successful, and thus is widely considered an automatic point gained in the game. Thus the expression means an action or procedure which is routinely performed and whose successful completion is taken for granted.